.TH TOPNG 1
.SH NAME
topng, tojpg \- a picture as PNG or JPEG
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B topng
.br
.B tojpg
[
.B -q
.I quality
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Topng
reads an
.IR image (6)
picture from its standard input and writes it on its standard output
as a PNG: 8-bit RGB, rows unfiltered, compressed with deflate.
.I Tojpg
writes a baseline JPEG instead, 4:2:0, at
.I quality
1 to 100 (85 if not given), through
.IR jpegenc (2).
.PP
An uncompressed r8g8b8 picture, as
.IR i420 (1)
writes, is taken as it is, with no display needed. Any other
.IR image (6)
picture, compressed or of other channels (a screen's, a window's),
is read through the draw device, which then has to be there.
.PP
Neither knows where the picture came from: they are the last link of a
pipe whose first is whatever makes pictures.
.SH EXAMPLES
A still from a camera:
.IP
.EX
read 189420 < /mnt/video/0/frame | i420 410 308 | topng > still.png
.EE
.PP
A smaller one:
.IP
.EX
read 189420 < /mnt/video/0/frame | i420 410 308 | tojpg -q 70 > still.jpg
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/topng.b
.br
.B /appl/cmd/tojpg.b
.br
.B /appl/lib/visrec.b
(the reading and the PNG)
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR i420 (1),
.IR camsrv (4),
.IR image (6),
.IR jpegenc (2)
